1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:03,819
On Mapping, read the warehouse call label
and open description

2
00:00:03,819 --> 00:00:05,539
before interpreting the marker.

3
00:00:05,940 --> 00:00:10,069
That popup identifies a fictional
incident; it does not establish

4
00:00:10,069 --> 00:00:12,239
where a person or apparatus is now.

5
00:00:12,739 --> 00:00:16,469
This walkthrough reviews Core
administration and recorded training data.

6
00:00:16,930 --> 00:00:20,590
Device permissions and field tracking need
their own application checks.

7
00:00:20,959 --> 00:00:25,540
Keep that distinction visible when using
location information for fire and EMS,

8
00:00:25,700 --> 00:00:28,360
community response, or industrial standby.

9
00:00:28,599 --> 00:00:33,869
In Department Settings, review Address and
Default Map Center GPS Coordinates.

10
00:00:34,210 --> 00:00:37,830
The paired latitude and longitude inputs
describe the starting map

11
00:00:37,830 --> 00:00:40,009
view, not a live vehicle fix.

12
00:00:40,360 --> 00:00:44,980
This example uses a fictional Chicago
address and explicit decimal coordinates.

13
00:00:45,310 --> 00:00:50,840
Check Street, City, State/Province,
Zip/Postal Code and Country

14
00:00:50,910 --> 00:00:52,580
before relying on the extent.

15
00:00:53,010 --> 00:00:57,299
Save and Cancel are visible; this
demonstration reads existing values

16
00:00:57,330 --> 00:00:59,219
and leaves the department unchanged.

17
00:00:59,389 --> 00:01:04,579
On Edit Group, confirm Station Group and
Group Name before reading Station Address.

18
00:01:05,059 --> 00:01:10,490
Firehouse 51 has a fictional Chicago
address and Gps Coordinates; the lower

19
00:01:10,490 --> 00:01:13,250
what3words Address field is empty.

20
00:01:13,599 --> 00:01:17,599
These are alternative station-location
inputs, not a live fix.

21
00:01:18,069 --> 00:01:21,079
Group Boundary is a separate response or
service area.

22
00:01:21,450 --> 00:01:25,280
This demonstration reads the existing
fields and preserves the station,

23
00:01:25,429 --> 00:01:27,870
boundary, apparatus assignment and crew.

24
00:01:28,109 --> 00:01:31,810
On Mapping, use Filter marker text to
focus the display.

25
00:01:32,179 --> 00:01:35,699
The retained Truck 81 view leaves that
named marker visible.

26
00:01:36,100 --> 00:01:40,800
Show calls, Show stations, Show units,
Show personnel and Show

27
00:01:40,800 --> 00:01:43,439
POIs control displayed categories.

28
00:01:43,800 --> 00:01:48,379
In the comparison view, the text filter is
empty and Show units is unchecked.

29
00:01:48,739 --> 00:01:52,559
A hidden category is not a released
resource or deleted position.

30
00:01:52,940 --> 00:01:56,750
Inspect these controls before treating an
expected resource as missing.

31
00:01:56,960 --> 00:02:01,720
From Mapping, Map Icon Legend explains
type and priority conventions.

32
00:02:02,170 --> 00:02:06,039
Routine, Urgent and Emergency appear in
separate columns.

33
00:02:06,499 --> 00:02:11,249
On Edit Call Type, the Structure Fire
Preview shows a stored custom icon and

34
00:02:11,249 --> 00:02:13,800
says Showing the current custom icon.

35
00:02:14,240 --> 00:02:16,949
The warehouse popup supplies the incident
description.

36
00:02:17,410 --> 00:02:19,349
These are visual identifiers.

37
00:02:19,570 --> 00:02:22,990
They do not establish a fresh position,
response acceptance

38
00:02:23,140 --> 00:02:24,570
or notification receipt.

39
00:02:24,980 --> 00:02:28,109
Read the label and context rather than
relying only on

40
00:02:28,109 --> 00:02:29,680
a flame or vehicle picture.

41
00:02:29,869 --> 00:02:32,830
On Mapping, the footer says Last update.

42
00:02:33,270 --> 00:02:36,749
It records when the client loaded or
refreshed marker data, or

43
00:02:36,749 --> 00:02:40,749
handled a location update; it is not every
resource’s fix time.

44
00:02:41,310 --> 00:02:45,690
In Units, Status and Timestamp belong to
the latest unit status.

45
00:02:46,020 --> 00:02:48,569
That time is not a GPS measurement either.

46
00:02:48,940 --> 00:02:51,489
These screens show historical training
states.

47
00:02:51,850 --> 00:02:55,190
Check the appropriate position source and
age before treating a

48
00:02:55,190 --> 00:02:59,309
page refresh or status entry as evidence
that an apparatus moved.

49
00:02:59,469 --> 00:03:04,070
In the recorded New Call position popup,
Engine 51 explicitly says

50
00:03:04,070 --> 00:03:08,190
Station location and shows station
coordinates beside the call location.

51
00:03:08,650 --> 00:03:11,169
That comparison uses a stored origin.

52
00:03:11,610 --> 00:03:15,589
A unit in quarters, or one without an
available live position, can

53
00:03:15,589 --> 00:03:18,790
be measured from its station under the
response-origin rules.

54
00:03:19,230 --> 00:03:21,450
Read the source before using the estimate.

55
00:03:21,849 --> 00:03:26,149
The displayed distance and time do not
prove physical presence, arrival,

56
00:03:26,239 --> 00:03:28,040
or an active navigation route.

57
00:03:28,160 --> 00:03:30,719
On New Call, compare the Personnel rows.

58
00:03:31,060 --> 00:03:35,920
One historical training view shows Live
GPS with a stale badge; the separately

59
00:03:35,920 --> 00:03:38,399
simulated newer view omits that badge.

60
00:03:38,859 --> 00:03:42,189
Live GPS names the application’s
data-source category.

61
00:03:42,510 --> 00:03:46,039
No real device permission or physical
movement was exercised.

62
00:03:46,410 --> 00:03:50,850
Status, Staffing, ETA and Position are
separate columns.

63
00:03:51,180 --> 00:03:55,879
Treat No position as missing information,
and review the source and configuration

64
00:03:55,879 --> 00:03:59,809
before using the first ranked candidate as
an operational recommendation.

65
00:04:00,029 --> 00:04:04,659
In Mapping and BigBoard Settings, review
personnel and unit controls separately.

66
00:04:05,159 --> 00:04:10,210
TTL In Minutes for Personnel Locations and
TTL In Minutes for Unit Locations

67
00:04:10,449 --> 00:04:12,439
both show zero in these views.

68
00:04:12,859 --> 00:04:18,969
Zero disables ping expiry; the help text’s
sixty-minute example is not a saved sixty.

69
00:04:19,379 --> 00:04:23,450
A location-bearing status can remain a
fallback after a ping expires.

70
00:04:23,840 --> 00:04:28,100
The separate no-location-status checkboxes
affect replacement behavior.

71
00:04:28,559 --> 00:04:31,620
Check the policy and position source
before promising that

72
00:04:31,620 --> 00:04:32,930
a marker will disappear.

73
00:04:33,069 --> 00:04:37,809
In dispatch settings, Closest Unit
Response Tuning has separate age controls.

74
00:04:38,210 --> 00:04:43,060
Maximum unit location age and Maximum
personnel location age are in seconds;

75
00:04:43,369 --> 00:04:45,630
both recorded values are eighteen hundred.

76
00:04:46,019 --> 00:04:48,850
They differ from map TTL measured in
minutes.

77
00:04:49,259 --> 00:04:51,640
Include stale locations is unchecked.

78
00:04:52,060 --> 00:04:56,609
Maximum response radius is zero, meaning
no configured maximum radius.

79
00:04:57,050 --> 00:04:59,660
These controls influence candidate
evaluation.

80
00:05:00,050 --> 00:05:03,849
They do not certify a fresh fix, prove
service-area coverage,

81
00:05:04,109 --> 00:05:07,100
or change a resource position because the
map refreshed.

82
00:05:07,319 --> 00:05:12,200
In the same Closest Unit Response Tuning
section, Order by driving ETA is

83
00:05:12,269 --> 00:05:15,679
unchecked and ETA shortlist size is five.

84
00:05:16,090 --> 00:05:21,059
Turnout is one hundred twenty seconds in
quarters, zero mobile and zero personnel.

85
00:05:21,540 --> 00:05:25,989
The matching Engine 51 station popup shows
a two-minute estimate including

86
00:05:25,989 --> 00:05:27,669
one hundred twenty seconds of turnout.

87
00:05:28,179 --> 00:05:31,460
Response combines applicable turnout with
estimated travel.

88
00:05:31,849 --> 00:05:33,400
Routed drive time is separate.

89
00:05:33,849 --> 00:05:37,560
This is no tested drive, confirmed
dispatch receipt, physical

90
00:05:37,560 --> 00:05:39,419
movement or arrival commitment.

91
00:05:39,670 --> 00:05:44,350
From Mapping, Manage POIs opens the empty
POI-type list.

92
00:05:44,739 --> 00:05:49,770
In Weather Alerts, Monitoring Zones offers
Center Location, Radius in miles

93
00:05:49,889 --> 00:05:52,520
and Save Zone; no zone is saved here.

94
00:05:52,919 --> 00:05:57,030
Hospitals, layers, floor plans and patrol
routes still require

95
00:05:57,030 --> 00:05:58,880
their own saved-workflow checks.

96
00:05:59,290 --> 00:06:03,200
For search and rescue, security, wildland
or community teams,

97
00:06:03,460 --> 00:06:07,050
apply the same source-and-age checks
before operational use.

98
00:06:07,390 --> 00:06:10,860
Keep missing reference data on the
follow-up list until its placement

99
00:06:10,890 --> 00:06:12,690
and limits are actually reviewed.

